id: twisted-trick
name: Twisted Trick
type: standard
actionCost: 1
kiCost: 0
attacking: false
requiresTarget: true
usageLimit: 1/round
# Opened while its Awakening applies (allow maneuver.<id>); a Special Maneuver, not a Villainous one - those every Adversary has.
special: true
source: Core Rule
description: >
  Target a foe, turning them into a target of trickery.
text: >
  Twisted Trick [1/Round]: Target a foe, turning them into a target of trickery.
  –Maneuver Type: Standard Maneuver
  –Action Cost: 1 Action
  –KP Cost: N/A
  –Exploitable: All Adjacent Opponents. If you take Damage from an Attacking Maneuver made through the Exploit Maneuver in response to this Attacking Maneuver, the Maneuver fails.
  –Effect: Target an Opponent and make a Clash (Cognitive/Morale) against them. If you win, that Opponent becomes a ‘Jinx’ until the end of the Combat Round.
  The Jinx and all of their Allies within a Large Sphere AoE of the Jinx, have their Critical Target and Botch Range swapped – meaning they score a Critical Result when they would score a Botch Result and vice versa.
  If the Jinx or any character affected by the AoE scores a Critical Result or a Botch Result, reduce their Life Points by your highest Attribute Modifier.

---

# Exploitable: whoever may Exploit it, and that a Damage taken from it makes it fail - the table's, as every Exploit is called.
# A Clash (Cognitive/Morale) at the target; won, the Jinx till the Round ends - its Critical and Botch swapped with its Allies in a
# Large Sphere, and Life Points lost by your highest Attribute Modifier on either: the table's (said on the card).
